// A contract member returning a type declared BESIDE the contract, implemented from another file in the
// SAME MODULE — which is what makes this reachable at all, since the import rung it trips is per-file
// and only exists inside a module.
//
// The contract's signature is rendered under the CONTRACT's own scope, so its imports are the ones
// consulted. Three sites did that swap by hand and all three moved three of `NsCtx`'s four fields,
// leaving `unitPath` pointing at the IMPLEMENTER. `checkReach` decides the rung by comparing exactly
// that path against the file being walked — precisely so it can tell "these imports belong to another
// file" — so the stale path made them agree, and `Thing` was judged against host.kama's imports. A file
// does not import what it declares, so impl.kama was told to import a name its own line 1 imports.
// Only a member returning a USER type could reach it: `plain()` below is the control.
export { Thing, Maker };

type value Thing {
    public int32 n;
    public ctor make(int32 n) { this.n = n; }
}

type contract Maker for value {
    fn Thing build();
    fn int32 plain();
}
